<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06SW">Remark <span data-tag="06SW">4.8.5.11</span>.</a> Let $n$ be an integer and let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a functor of $\infty $-categories which can be realized as the colimit of a filtered diagram $\{  F_{\alpha }: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{\alpha } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{\alpha } \} $ in the category $\operatorname{Fun}( [1], \operatorname{Set_{\Delta }})$. If each $F_{\alpha }$ is a categorically $n$-connective functor of $\infty $-categories, then $F$ is a categorically $n$-connective functor of $\infty $-categories. See Remark <a data-tag="06S8" href="/tag/06S8">4.8.2.12</a>. </p>
</article>
